      "text": "BAMAKO — Convoy movement was reported along the RN17 corridor south of Gao on Tuesday, according to three residents reached by telephone in Ansongo and Bourem. A regional official in Mopti, speaking on condition of anonymity, said the column crossed the Niger near Labbezanga before dispersing east toward Ménaka.\n\nAid workers in Niamey confirmed the suspension of overland transport into Tillabéri. Reports circulating on local messaging channels place a second group near Kidal, roughly 40 km north-east of the Tessalit road junction, though the claim could not be independently verified.\n\nA statement issued from Ouagadougou made no reference to the movement.",
